The fix: /run used to read all output before checking whether the shell had exited. Now run_shell_command reads stdout and stderr on separate threads and waits for the shell itself. Once the shell exits, it gives those threads up to 2 seconds to finish (the new RUN_READER_GRACE constant). The doc comment on that constant points at the same 2-second wait in the model's bash tool in src/tools.rs.

Run against the built binary:
• yoyo run 'sleep 6 & echo hi' printed hi, then a dim note that a background process still holds the output, then ✓ exit 0 (2.0s). Total time was 2.0s; before the fix it was 6.0s.
• echo a; sleep 0.3; echo b; exit 3 still showed both lines and reported exit 3 in 302ms, so commands that don't start a background job behave as before.

Checklist:
• Tests: all the requested ones are there, plus two more: a background job holding only stderr, and CRLF / unfinished-last-line handling matching the old BufRead::lines() reader.
• Forgotten touchpoints: every new definition (the constant, the StreamTap struct and its methods, the ReaderHandle type, spawn_stream_reader) is used in this diff. There are no new enum variants.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md gained a sentence about backgrounded jobs that matches what the binary actually prints.
• Product surface: no defaults, CLI flags or startup behaviour changed.

